1
00:00:07,549 --> 00:00:09,342
PROXY

2
00:00:09,343 --> 00:00:12,387
[pensive music playing]

3
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:22,188
Sign the proxy over to me.

4
00:00:22,189 --> 00:00:23,482
Let me vote on your behalf

5
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:26,568
to decide Chang Xin's future.

6
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:35,493
Your dad did the wrong things
in the first place.

7
00:00:35,494 --> 00:00:37,704
You shouldn't be the one
paying the price.

8
00:00:45,504 --> 00:00:47,798
You want me to vote
for your market faction?

9
00:00:50,259 --> 00:00:51,593
Go to hell.

10
00:00:52,219 --> 00:00:53,595
I won't betray my dad.

11
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:58,141
- But your dad betrayed you.
- He did not.

12
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:02,563
He needs to hold
onto the company,
so he's able to protect me.

13
00:01:02,688 --> 00:01:05,524
- Don't you get it?
- [laughs]

14
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:07,359
Sorry.

15
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:13,240
If you like laughing so much,
go home and laugh
all you want.

16
00:01:13,365 --> 00:01:14,741
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

17
00:01:16,118 --> 00:01:17,494
I'm so sorry.

18
00:01:19,371 --> 00:01:21,289
I just think

19
00:01:21,290 --> 00:01:23,499
your dad has trained you
really well.

20
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,546
Before he finds
an excuse for you,
you've got a reason for him.

21
00:01:27,671 --> 00:01:30,382
He doesn't find
an excuse for me.

22
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:33,552
He needs to hold
onto Chang Xin
to promise me a future.

23
00:01:38,307 --> 00:01:40,349
Listen to me.

24
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:42,768
Your dad will come
to visit you soon.

25
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:46,106
Then he'll try to convince you
with what you've told me.

26
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:48,442
And he'll want you
to sign the proxy.

27
00:01:58,493 --> 00:02:00,120
Actually,
I don't need to tell you.

28
00:02:00,245 --> 00:02:03,831
You know well
what your dad will say.

29
00:02:03,832 --> 00:02:05,125
Don't you?

30
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:16,887
If I do that, what do I get?

31
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:23,894
When you're released,
I'll do my best
to get you a position.

32
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:26,563
[laughs] Is that all?

33
00:02:30,776 --> 00:02:33,445
Why do you think
I still care about that?

34
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:35,238
Yes, you do.

35
00:02:37,949 --> 00:02:41,619
Have you really thought
about what kind of person
you want to be?

36
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:42,954
Do you respect yourself?

37
00:02:45,624 --> 00:02:47,876
Let me ask you
one more question.

38
00:02:50,337 --> 00:02:53,965
All these years,
has your dad seen you as a son,

39
00:02:55,467 --> 00:02:57,302
or as a pawn?

40
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:07,646
[singer] <i>♪ Someday, you can
Find sunshine, sunshine ♪</i>

41
00:03:07,771 --> 00:03:12,316
[singing in Mandarin]

42
00:03:12,317 --> 00:03:14,652
<i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

43
00:03:14,653 --> 00:03:16,655
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

44
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,906
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

45
00:03:18,907 --> 00:03:20,867
[singing in Mandarin]

46
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:25,163
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

47
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:27,916
[singing in Mandarin]

48
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:36,340
The vote is close,
but with our secured votes
we are still slightly behind.

49
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:38,844
We can only rely
on that 5% of swing votes.

50
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:41,512
Do you know
what the scariest thing is?

51
00:03:41,513 --> 00:03:43,431
Chairman Chang still has cards
to play up to the last minute,

52
00:03:43,432 --> 00:03:44,891
while we have no tricks
up our sleeves.

53
00:03:49,271 --> 00:03:52,315
[tense music playing]

54
00:03:54,735 --> 00:03:55,902
[Chin-nan]
<i>What are you doing here?</i>

55
00:04:04,828 --> 00:04:07,622
[singer] <i>♪ Nobody knows ♪</i>

56
00:04:08,874 --> 00:04:11,710
<i>♪ Nobody, nobody knows me ♪</i>

57
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:16,547
I've got
Chang Chien-yuan's proxy.

58
00:04:16,548 --> 00:04:18,884
[singer]
<i>♪ Nobody, nobody knows me ♪</i>

59
00:04:19,009 --> 00:04:20,844
Hi.

60
00:04:20,969 --> 00:04:23,721
What's going on? I don't get it.

61
00:04:23,722 --> 00:04:25,931
Yeah, what's going on?

62
00:04:25,932 --> 00:04:28,392
I went undercover
in your family.

63
00:04:28,393 --> 00:04:30,437
How were my acting skills?

64
00:04:31,396 --> 00:04:34,316
<i>Wait, Lu-yung,
did you know that?</i>

65
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,943
I found out not long ago.

66
00:04:38,862 --> 00:04:40,447
Give me the list
of your faction's shareholders.

67
00:04:40,572 --> 00:04:44,034
[tense music playing]

68
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:47,496
[singer singing
foreign language]

69
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:54,461
TRUST ME.

70
00:04:54,586 --> 00:04:56,046
[Yi-hsuan] Give me the list.

71
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:03,804
[singer]
<i>♪ 'Cause nobody knows ♪</i>

72
00:05:03,929 --> 00:05:05,305
Welcome back to Jin Lai Hao.

73
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:11,061
<i>Great. Chang Chien-yuan
is a major shareholder.</i>

74
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:14,606
With his votes,
we'll be much more likely
to turn the tables.

75
00:05:14,731 --> 00:05:16,608
<i>Good job. Thank you.</i>

76
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:18,776
Whoa!

77
00:05:18,777 --> 00:05:22,530
You even tricked me, young lady.
Good job.

78
00:05:22,531 --> 00:05:23,949
Damn! That's cool!

79
00:05:24,074 --> 00:05:25,617
[laughs]

80
00:05:25,742 --> 00:05:30,121
Chao Yi-hsuan, you're bad.
You only told Boss.

81
00:05:30,997 --> 00:05:32,457
I'm sorry, babe.

82
00:05:33,083 --> 00:05:34,459
[groans]

83
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:36,628
It was hard for me
to keep the secret.

84
00:05:36,753 --> 00:05:39,422
Had no choice.
The fewer people who knew,
the better.

85
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:42,008
At least, I'm back now. Right?

86
00:05:42,133 --> 00:05:43,717
[laughter]

87
00:05:43,718 --> 00:05:44,970
[Yu-li] Right!

88
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,849
[singer vocalizing]

89
00:05:49,516 --> 00:05:51,518
[Yu-li] Missed you!

90
00:05:51,643 --> 00:05:53,687
Good job!

91
00:05:53,812 --> 00:05:55,856
- [Feng] <i>That's cool! We'll win!</i>
- [Lu-yung] <i>Jin Lai Hao...</i>

92
00:05:56,481 --> 00:05:57,983
Go!

93
00:05:58,775 --> 00:06:00,734
[Feng] We'll win.

94
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:02,070
See you tomorrow.

95
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:05,489
Be careful.

96
00:06:05,490 --> 00:06:08,994
[indistinct chatter]

97
00:06:09,119 --> 00:06:11,079
- [Yu-li] Bye.
- [Lu-yung] Get home safe.

98
00:06:11,997 --> 00:06:13,665
[Yu-li] Bye!

99
00:06:22,716 --> 00:06:23,842
[Secretary Chin] Chien-wu?

100
00:06:30,557 --> 00:06:32,475
Your dad doesn't have much time.

101
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:34,853
He wants to see you.

102
00:06:37,606 --> 00:06:38,940
What does that mean?

103
00:06:42,694 --> 00:06:45,196
[gentle music playing]

104
00:06:49,034 --> 00:06:52,078
[insects trilling]

105
00:06:54,789 --> 00:06:57,750
What's going on, Dad?
What do you mean
you don't have much time?

106
00:06:57,751 --> 00:06:59,878
Didn't the doctor say
it was nothing serious?

107
00:07:02,589 --> 00:07:06,551
Chien-wu,
terminal pancreatic cancer,
spread to the liver and lungs.

108
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:09,054
He has three months left,
maybe less.

109
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:13,850
He has something to tell you.

110
00:07:20,732 --> 00:07:22,776
I found out last year.

111
00:07:25,195 --> 00:07:27,948
I wanted to fight against it.

112
00:07:32,786 --> 00:07:34,162
However,

113
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:37,540
I lost the battle.

114
00:07:42,712 --> 00:07:46,591
It pains me that
I've worked hard for Chang Xin
for a lifetime,

115
00:07:48,802 --> 00:07:51,096
and now it'll soon belong
to someone else.

116
00:07:53,765 --> 00:07:55,558
You've done a good job.

117
00:07:57,143 --> 00:07:58,770
You've listened to me

118
00:07:59,813 --> 00:08:01,481
and cut ties with me completely.

119
00:08:02,774 --> 00:08:04,192
You haven't been soft-hearted.

120
00:08:05,652 --> 00:08:07,278
You've really done a good job.

121
00:08:07,946 --> 00:08:09,114
[chuckles]

122
00:08:13,618 --> 00:08:16,121
But I know I'm not a good dad.

123
00:08:17,706 --> 00:08:19,666
I don't have much time left.

124
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:23,044
All I can teach you

125
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:26,631
is how to do business well.

126
00:08:26,756 --> 00:08:28,048
[cries]

127
00:08:28,049 --> 00:08:30,802
[Chang Ta-chin]
So, remember every word

128
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:32,219
that I'm going to tell you.

129
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:35,265
[sobbing]

130
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:40,979
When we do business,

131
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:47,193
we deal with things
in ways people might not
understand or agree with.

132
00:08:50,113 --> 00:08:51,906
But that's called vision.

133
00:08:53,825 --> 00:08:55,285
For that,

134
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:59,205
I've never asked anyone
to understand me.

135
00:09:01,041 --> 00:09:04,627
I knew it was bound to succeed,
so I needed to persist.

136
00:09:10,008 --> 00:09:11,593
But Chiang Shu-min

137
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:13,927
knows nothing at all.

138
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:16,930
All she wants is to replace me.

139
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:20,100
I know she's planning
to get rid of me

140
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:23,605
and kick me out at the meeting.

141
00:09:28,777 --> 00:09:30,195
She's wrong.

142
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:35,784
She never thought that

143
00:09:37,035 --> 00:09:41,081
my son stated clearly
in the magazine that

144
00:09:41,206 --> 00:09:44,291
he has cut all ties
with his dad.

145
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:47,712
Even if I've done
something terribly wrong,

146
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:49,255
it has nothing to do
with my son.

147
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:53,258
She'll never defile my son.

148
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:54,886
[laughs]

149
00:09:58,306 --> 00:09:59,682
No, she won't.

150
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:06,356
[water pattering]

151
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:10,944
[tense music playing]

152
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:17,659
Dad.

153
00:10:25,125 --> 00:10:27,000
Go away!

154
00:10:27,001 --> 00:10:28,628
Leave me alone.

155
00:10:30,213 --> 00:10:31,422
For your future,

156
00:10:32,423 --> 00:10:33,925
you need to

157
00:10:35,009 --> 00:10:36,261
cut ties with me completely.

158
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:38,763
From now on,

159
00:10:40,098 --> 00:10:41,850
we'll never see
each other again.

160
00:10:46,396 --> 00:10:48,106
And don't even...

161
00:10:50,275 --> 00:10:51,818
attend my funeral.

162
00:10:52,235 --> 00:10:53,778
What are you talking about, Dad?

163
00:10:53,903 --> 00:10:55,822
- Did you hear me?
- What are you talking about?

164
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:01,327
[sighs]

165
00:11:01,452 --> 00:11:03,288
- Get out.
- No.

166
00:11:03,413 --> 00:11:04,455
- Out.
- No.

167
00:11:04,706 --> 00:11:05,789
- Out!
- No!

168
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:06,957
[Chang Ta-chin] Secretary Chin!

169
00:11:06,958 --> 00:11:08,293
Sir?

170
00:11:08,418 --> 00:11:10,127
[Chang Ta-chin] Out!

171
00:11:10,128 --> 00:11:11,837
[Secretary Chin]
Please leave, Chien-wu.

172
00:11:11,838 --> 00:11:14,966
- [cries]
- [sighs]

173
00:11:16,926 --> 00:11:18,344
[Chang Ta-chin groans]

174
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:28,354
[whimpers]

175
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:31,733
[door closes]

176
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:37,655
[sobbing]

177
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:40,658
[dramatic music playing]

178
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:42,744
[birds chirping]

179
00:11:56,799 --> 00:11:57,967
Please, sir.

180
00:12:09,437 --> 00:12:10,939
[sighs]

181
00:12:13,358 --> 00:12:16,027
[indistinct chatter]

182
00:12:16,152 --> 00:12:17,946
Good morning. This way, please.

183
00:12:22,075 --> 00:12:24,284
- [Shu-min] Thank you.
- [Mr. Chen] No problem.

184
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:25,954
- [Lu-yung] Hi, Miss Chiang.
- Hey.

185
00:12:26,537 --> 00:12:27,872
Are you nervous?

186
00:12:29,916 --> 00:12:31,793
I was worried
something unexpected
might happen,

187
00:12:33,211 --> 00:12:34,712
but it looks calm.

188
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:35,879
[Shu-min] Don't worry.

189
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:37,298
Let's welcome our victory.

190
00:12:39,092 --> 00:12:40,218
Let's go.

191
00:12:43,846 --> 00:12:44,931
[elevator dings]

192
00:12:51,938 --> 00:12:55,316
[suspenseful music playing]

193
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:30,225
[Secretary Chin]
See you later, ma'am.

194
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:32,269
[press] Long time, sir.
How are you feeling?

195
00:13:32,270 --> 00:13:33,604
[Chang Ta-chin] Thank you.

196
00:13:33,855 --> 00:13:35,440
- [press] Feeling better?
- [Chang Ta-chin] Yes.

197
00:13:37,108 --> 00:13:39,109
- [Secretary Chin] Be careful.
- Thank you.

198
00:13:39,110 --> 00:13:41,154
[overlapping chatter]

199
00:13:44,574 --> 00:13:47,160
- [press]
Sir, regarding today's vote...
- Be careful.

200
00:13:47,285 --> 00:13:49,454
- Thank you.
- [Secretary Chin] Be careful.

201
00:13:49,579 --> 00:13:52,164
[press] Are you confident
about today's vote, sir?

202
00:13:52,165 --> 00:13:53,958
[music continues]

203
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:08,639
[Secretary Chin] Excuse us.
Coming through. Thank you.

204
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:10,182
Thank you.

205
00:14:10,183 --> 00:14:12,018
[camera shutters clicking]

206
00:14:27,909 --> 00:14:29,869
I'm sorry,

207
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:31,996
but he's my dad after all.

208
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:34,332
Chang Xin is his life.

209
00:14:36,876 --> 00:14:39,087
I need to protect his dignity
one last time.

210
00:14:56,521 --> 00:14:58,064
We've lost.

211
00:14:58,189 --> 00:15:01,192
[applause]

212
00:15:06,406 --> 00:15:08,448
[Secretary Chin] <i>Do you think</i>

213
00:15:08,449 --> 00:15:10,117
<i>Chien-wu will...</i>

214
00:15:10,118 --> 00:15:11,869
[Chang Ta-chin]
<i>He'll come back.</i>

215
00:15:11,994 --> 00:15:13,996
I know my own son well.

216
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,417
He's good at everything

217
00:15:18,418 --> 00:15:20,169
except for one weakness.

218
00:15:21,587 --> 00:15:23,589
He's softhearted.

219
00:15:23,714 --> 00:15:27,260
[applause]

220
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:31,055
[Lu-yung sighs, tongue clicks]

221
00:15:37,228 --> 00:15:40,273
[pensive music playing]

222
00:15:44,986 --> 00:15:46,446
What's going on?

223
00:15:46,571 --> 00:15:49,240
[applause]

224
00:15:54,579 --> 00:15:57,373
[indistinct chatter]

225
00:16:00,376 --> 00:16:02,335
I'm from the Taipei District
Prosecutors Office.

226
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:03,713
I'm Prosecutor Chang.

227
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:06,089
You're suspected of forgery,

228
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:07,717
multiple counts
of importing ingredients
that violate food safety,

229
00:16:08,092 --> 00:16:10,177
bribery,
and incitement to murder.

230
00:16:10,178 --> 00:16:13,305
We're bringing you in
to assist in the investigation.
Please cooperate.

231
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:14,974
This is your arrest warrant.

232
00:16:16,476 --> 00:16:18,268
Come on. Cuff him.
Take him away.

233
00:16:18,269 --> 00:16:19,937
[reporter] <i>Breaking news.</i>

234
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:22,481
<i>Chang Xin's tainted
oil scandal from years ago</i>

235
00:16:22,482 --> 00:16:24,566
<i>has taken a dramatic turn.</i>

236
00:16:24,567 --> 00:16:27,737
<i>Former head chef,
Chou Chin-lai,
was accused back then.</i>

237
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:32,199
<i>But further investigation
reveals that
his signature was forged.</i>

238
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:35,786
<i>And the mastermind behind
everything is very likely
Chairman Chang Ta-chin.</i>

239
00:16:36,037 --> 00:16:38,330
<i>He is suspected of forgery</i>

240
00:16:38,331 --> 00:16:41,291
<i>and multiple counts
of importing ingredients
that violate food safety.</i>

241
00:16:41,292 --> 00:16:42,627
<i>According to some information,</i>

242
00:16:42,752 --> 00:16:44,628
<i>former Speaker
Chong Cheng-chiang</i>

243
00:16:44,629 --> 00:16:46,464
<i>and owner of
Ding Xiong Construction,</i>

244
00:16:46,589 --> 00:16:48,757
<i>Tsao Yi-cheng,
were also involved.</i>

245
00:16:48,758 --> 00:16:50,968
<i>They're both
under investigation now.</i>

246
00:16:51,093 --> 00:16:55,347
<i>We'll bring you live updates
when there is
new information.</i>

247
00:16:55,348 --> 00:16:58,142
[rock music playing]

248
00:17:04,649 --> 00:17:08,652
[Feng] Boss,
I still can't believe the head
of such a large corporation

249
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:10,488
like Chang Ta-chin
just collapsed.

250
00:17:10,613 --> 00:17:14,158
I think he deserves it.
Serves him right.

251
00:17:16,118 --> 00:17:19,830
I think the prosecutors
have got some new evidence.

252
00:17:20,081 --> 00:17:21,164
[Feng] He's doomed.

253
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:22,708
And it's time!

254
00:17:23,543 --> 00:17:25,419
Sorry, but we're closed.

255
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:30,716
Long time no see.

256
00:17:30,841 --> 00:17:32,343
Your hair is still
as cool as ever.

257
00:17:33,678 --> 00:17:36,138
You're Chang Chien-yuan's
best pal.

258
00:17:37,598 --> 00:17:39,349
Damn! What are you doing here?

259
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:41,226
Wait.

260
00:17:41,227 --> 00:17:44,480
No need to be so hostile, okay?
I'm here to deliver a letter.

261
00:17:46,774 --> 00:17:48,025
Not for you.

262
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:50,194
Mr. Chou Lu-yung, it's for you.

263
00:17:51,237 --> 00:17:53,364
Miss Wu Hsiu-wen asked me
to give it to you.

264
00:17:57,201 --> 00:17:58,327
Hsiu-wen?

265
00:18:09,839 --> 00:18:12,091
TO: LU-YUNG

266
00:18:13,718 --> 00:18:15,386
[Hsiu-wen] <i>Hi, Chou Lu-yung.</i>

267
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:20,640
<i>I'm used
to writing letters to you.</i>

268
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:22,726
<i>At this moment,</i>

269
00:18:22,727 --> 00:18:25,229
<i>I don't know
the results of your
shareholders' meeting.</i>

270
00:18:26,272 --> 00:18:27,898
<i>But when you get the letter,</i>

271
00:18:28,149 --> 00:18:30,234
<i>I believe everything
will have been settled.</i>

272
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:33,653
<i>Now,</i>

273
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:35,781
<i>you must be confused.</i>

274
00:18:37,867 --> 00:18:39,910
<i>Remember when I graduated
from grad school,</i>

275
00:18:40,161 --> 00:18:41,787
<i>and was planning
to study abroad?</i>

276
00:18:43,164 --> 00:18:45,332
<i>But when I saw the news
about Uncle Chin-lai,</i>

277
00:18:45,333 --> 00:18:46,791
<i>I changed my plans.</i>

278
00:18:46,792 --> 00:18:49,128
[reporter] <i>...the person
in charge of the oil</i>

279
00:18:49,253 --> 00:18:51,464
<i>was their former Research
and Development Chef,
Chou Chin-lai.</i>

280
00:18:51,589 --> 00:18:53,298
<i>He violated
the company's regulations</i>

281
00:18:53,299 --> 00:18:56,468
<i>and insisted on using cheap,
low-quality oil.</i>

282
00:18:56,469 --> 00:19:00,597
<i>But Chou Chin-lai
died six years ago.</i>

283
00:19:00,598 --> 00:19:04,310
<i>I know it was impossible that
Uncle Chin-lai had done that.</i>

284
00:19:05,770 --> 00:19:08,688
<i>So, I decided to stay
to find out the truth.</i>

285
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:11,776
[pensive music playing]

286
00:19:19,325 --> 00:19:22,285
[Hsiu-wen] <i>But at first,
I was a nobody,</i>

287
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:24,496
<i>who couldn't access
confidential information.</i>

288
00:19:24,497 --> 00:19:26,540
[camera shutters clicking]

289
00:19:28,209 --> 00:19:31,253
[laughter]

290
00:19:35,591 --> 00:19:37,677
[Hsiu-wen] <i>So I turned
to Chang Chien-yuan.</i>

291
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:49,605
[indistinct chatter]

292
00:19:54,318 --> 00:19:57,613
<i>In no time,
Po became his best pal
and earned his trust.</i>

293
00:20:02,827 --> 00:20:03,910
What did you say?

294
00:20:03,911 --> 00:20:06,455
Yeah. I killed him.

295
00:20:08,290 --> 00:20:11,918
...you as the future boss
of Chang Xin.

296
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:13,879
- That's enough.
- Feel it.

297
00:20:15,756 --> 00:20:16,965
- [Po] Like this?
- Yeah.

298
00:20:16,966 --> 00:20:19,343
[Po] Cool!
Your dad is so with you.

299
00:20:26,267 --> 00:20:29,394
[Chien-wu] <i>He just skidded.
I was right up on his tail...</i>

300
00:20:29,395 --> 00:20:31,188
<i>...and crashed down
the riverbank.</i>

301
00:20:31,313 --> 00:20:33,232
<i>And Chou Chin-lai...</i>

302
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:34,733
[Po] <i>What?</i>

303
00:20:34,734 --> 00:20:36,609
[Chien-wu] <i>He died!</i>

304
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:38,529
- [Po] <i>For real?</i>
- [Chien-wu] <i>Yeah.</i>

305
00:20:38,654 --> 00:20:40,906
<i>It was all just fate.</i>

306
00:20:41,031 --> 00:20:42,366
<i>Simple as that.</i>

307
00:20:46,287 --> 00:20:48,371
[Hsiu-wen] <i>Even though
Chang Chien-yuan was in jail,</i>

308
00:20:48,372 --> 00:20:52,626
<i>the real culprit
behind everything
was still at large.</i>

309
00:20:56,338 --> 00:21:01,010
While Chien-yuan is absent,
you take over his job.

310
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:06,807
[Hsiu-wen] <i>I finally gained
top-level authorization</i>

311
00:21:08,058 --> 00:21:09,768
<i>and found the key evidence</i>

312
00:21:09,769 --> 00:21:11,979
<i>that Chang Ta-chin
had framed Uncle Chin-lai.</i>

313
00:21:16,901 --> 00:21:19,403
CHOU CHIN-LAI

314
00:21:19,528 --> 00:21:22,323
[uplifting music playing]

315
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:36,628
[Hsiu-wen] <i>I submitted all the
information of Chang Xin's
illegal activities</i>

316
00:21:36,629 --> 00:21:38,506
<i>over the years
to the prosecutors.</i>

317
00:21:43,844 --> 00:21:46,847
[camera shutters clicking]

318
00:21:56,023 --> 00:22:00,652
[Hsiu-wen] <i>I didn't do it
for you, but for myself</i>

319
00:22:00,653 --> 00:22:02,613
<i>and my promise
to Uncle Chin-lai.</i>

320
00:22:03,697 --> 00:22:06,534
[birds chirping]

321
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:14,082
Happy birthday.

322
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:16,919
So thick? Don't tell me
they're all 100-dollar bills.

323
00:22:18,921 --> 00:22:20,672
If they're 1000-dollar bills,
I'll gladly accept them.

324
00:22:20,673 --> 00:22:21,966
Open it to take a look.

325
00:22:26,387 --> 00:22:27,887
No. It's too much.
I can't take it.

326
00:22:27,888 --> 00:22:31,475
But you just said
you'd gladly accept them.

327
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:33,143
No. I can't take it.

328
00:22:33,394 --> 00:22:34,937
Try to convince me.

329
00:22:36,772 --> 00:22:38,731
Okay.

330
00:22:38,732 --> 00:22:40,860
First, you were just fired.

331
00:22:40,985 --> 00:22:42,819
No.

332
00:22:42,820 --> 00:22:44,655
I fired them.

333
00:22:45,656 --> 00:22:46,906
Fine.

334
00:22:46,907 --> 00:22:49,826
Have you got
enough money for retirement?

335
00:22:49,827 --> 00:22:51,161
How old are you? Besides...

336
00:22:51,412 --> 00:22:52,997
I'm not old at all.

337
00:22:53,122 --> 00:22:56,667
I'm still healthy.
I'm starting up my own business.

338
00:22:56,792 --> 00:22:58,585
So you need money
to open a restaurant.

339
00:22:58,586 --> 00:23:01,588
I've got that money planned out.

340
00:23:01,589 --> 00:23:04,425
This has nothing
to do with that.

341
00:23:06,385 --> 00:23:08,012
Okay. Second?

342
00:23:12,892 --> 00:23:14,768
I owe you too much.

343
00:23:19,148 --> 00:23:20,691
I don't like it.

344
00:23:26,447 --> 00:23:27,531
Don't like what?

345
00:23:28,824 --> 00:23:30,534
Being patronized?

346
00:23:30,659 --> 00:23:33,704
[gentle music playing]

347
00:23:38,167 --> 00:23:39,919
[sighs]

348
00:23:42,546 --> 00:23:44,673
I'll lend you the money then.

349
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:48,594
When you begin to earn a living
after graduation,

350
00:23:48,719 --> 00:23:50,137
you'll pay me back.

351
00:23:54,183 --> 00:23:55,476
Fine.

352
00:23:56,769 --> 00:23:59,687
I'll consider the money
your investment in me.

353
00:23:59,688 --> 00:24:01,815
When I begin to earn a living,
I'll pay you back double.

354
00:24:02,983 --> 00:24:04,108
Double?

355
00:24:04,109 --> 00:24:05,444
Okay.

356
00:24:06,987 --> 00:24:09,155
- High return on investment,
right?
- [laughs]

357
00:24:09,156 --> 00:24:11,033
No, I want triple.

358
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:13,576
Triple is too much.
That's not reasonable.

359
00:24:13,577 --> 00:24:14,620
It's reasonable.

360
00:24:17,122 --> 00:24:18,998
Because...

361
00:24:18,999 --> 00:24:21,001
you're better than you think.

362
00:24:25,589 --> 00:24:27,091
You deserve a better future.

363
00:24:34,098 --> 00:24:35,265
Thank you, Uncle.

364
00:24:35,516 --> 00:24:38,268
[gentle music playing]

365
00:24:48,779 --> 00:24:51,907
[Hsiu-wen] <i>From now on,
I'll live for myself.</i>

366
00:24:53,242 --> 00:24:56,787
<i>To be honest,
I still don't know how
to navigate my path ahead.</i>

367
00:24:58,747 --> 00:25:00,708
<i>Maybe I'll write
to you again.</i>

368
00:25:01,959 --> 00:25:04,920
<i>Or maybe, this is
my last letter to you.</i>

369
00:25:07,256 --> 00:25:09,299
<i>Can you root for me
as a friend?</i>

370
00:25:12,553 --> 00:25:14,263
<i>Chou Lu-yung,</i>

371
00:25:14,513 --> 00:25:17,641
<i>cherish the present moment
and the people around you.</i>

372
00:25:19,643 --> 00:25:21,853
<i>I hope that from now on,</i>

373
00:25:21,854 --> 00:25:24,189
<i>we can move on
with our lives.</i>

374
00:25:35,659 --> 00:25:37,703
Sorry. I forgot something.

375
00:25:38,537 --> 00:25:39,830
[Lu-yung] Hmm?

376
00:25:52,092 --> 00:25:53,260
What?

377
00:26:01,060 --> 00:26:02,936
Aren't you leaving?

378
00:26:07,024 --> 00:26:08,734
I want to stay a little longer.

379
00:26:10,319 --> 00:26:11,695
Are you in a hurry?

380
00:26:13,655 --> 00:26:15,866
[gentle music playing]

381
00:26:33,008 --> 00:26:34,343
Are you alright?

382
00:26:38,263 --> 00:26:39,389
I'm fine.

383
00:26:40,724 --> 00:26:42,726
But I think

384
00:26:42,851 --> 00:26:44,353
I've gotten
to know myself better.

385
00:26:45,854 --> 00:26:47,022
What does that mean?

386
00:26:50,651 --> 00:26:52,611
Hsiu-wen told me

387
00:26:52,736 --> 00:26:54,279
to cherish the people I love.

388
00:27:00,285 --> 00:27:01,870
[sighs]

389
00:27:03,831 --> 00:27:05,958
She finally said
something decent.

390
00:27:07,126 --> 00:27:08,961
[chuckling]

391
00:27:09,086 --> 00:27:11,630
Why are you giggling?
What's so funny?

392
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:29,356
[chuckling]

393
00:27:37,948 --> 00:27:40,993
[laughter]

394
00:27:45,664 --> 00:27:48,709
[phone buzzing]

395
00:27:52,796 --> 00:27:54,298
It's Chang Ta-chin.

396
00:27:59,094 --> 00:28:02,014
Looks like we've got
some problems to solve.

397
00:28:09,730 --> 00:28:11,190
[sighs]

398
00:28:15,194 --> 00:28:16,987
[Chang Ta-chin] You're talented,

399
00:28:18,363 --> 00:28:20,157
good at cooking like your dad.

400
00:28:21,283 --> 00:28:22,993
[laughs]

401
00:28:26,288 --> 00:28:28,874
We're going to rename
Chang Xin, and that's why
you called us here, right?

402
00:28:32,085 --> 00:28:34,171
Director Chiang and I
will come up with a better name.

403
00:28:34,796 --> 00:28:35,881
Don't worry.

404
00:28:43,222 --> 00:28:44,473
[sighs]

405
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:45,807
Leave us.

406
00:28:50,270 --> 00:28:51,813
[groans]

407
00:29:01,198 --> 00:29:03,200
[groans]

408
00:29:06,119 --> 00:29:07,829
[sharp inhales]

409
00:29:09,122 --> 00:29:11,875
[labored breathing]

410
00:29:17,923 --> 00:29:19,424
Could you please...

411
00:29:21,218 --> 00:29:22,552
not rename Chang Xin?

412
00:29:23,929 --> 00:29:25,055
Because of you,

413
00:29:26,807 --> 00:29:29,809
so many bad things
have happened to Chang Xin.

414
00:29:29,810 --> 00:29:31,728
We'll have to rename it.

415
00:29:31,853 --> 00:29:34,523
Chang Xin
is in terrible shape now.

416
00:29:35,983 --> 00:29:39,069
What good does it do you
to acquire it?

417
00:29:40,153 --> 00:29:41,905
Because it's still essentially
a good company.

418
00:29:43,282 --> 00:29:44,491
This is purely
a business decision.

419
00:29:46,243 --> 00:29:49,121
[dramatic music playing]

420
00:29:49,246 --> 00:29:51,039
[sighing]

421
00:30:07,514 --> 00:30:08,807
Lu-yung,

422
00:30:12,102 --> 00:30:14,104
I'm dying.

423
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:18,358
I really want
to make an apology.

424
00:30:19,443 --> 00:30:22,445
I shouldn't have done
all those evil things

425
00:30:22,446 --> 00:30:24,114
to you and your dad.

426
00:30:25,824 --> 00:30:27,075
It's my fault.

427
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:29,328
All my fault.

428
00:30:32,914 --> 00:30:34,416
But Chang Xin...

429
00:30:36,001 --> 00:30:37,836
Chang Xin is my life.

430
00:30:39,338 --> 00:30:40,464
Please.

431
00:30:41,882 --> 00:30:42,966
Don't rename it.

432
00:30:44,843 --> 00:30:45,969
Please.

433
00:30:47,095 --> 00:30:48,847
Please.

434
00:30:50,140 --> 00:30:51,266
Please.

435
00:30:52,893 --> 00:30:54,102
I'm begging you.

436
00:30:55,979 --> 00:30:57,480
I'm begging you.

437
00:30:57,481 --> 00:30:58,565
Don't rename it.

438
00:31:08,533 --> 00:31:09,868
Chang Ta-chin.

439
00:31:11,370 --> 00:31:13,914
- [cries]
- [knocks on floor]

440
00:31:16,333 --> 00:31:19,461
Didn't you want to know
why exactly I went
to work at Chang Xin?

441
00:31:21,338 --> 00:31:22,464
Hmm?

442
00:31:25,425 --> 00:31:26,927
Because I wanted to see

443
00:31:28,095 --> 00:31:30,389
if you're worthy
to be my father.

444
00:31:31,515 --> 00:31:34,017
[music intensifies]

445
00:31:42,484 --> 00:31:44,444
Do you remember this earring?

446
00:31:47,614 --> 00:31:49,491
Huh?

447
00:31:53,912 --> 00:31:55,539
[chuckles]

448
00:31:58,208 --> 00:31:59,292
Too bad.

449
00:32:00,585 --> 00:32:02,212
You've forgotten her.

450
00:32:04,089 --> 00:32:05,215
Haven't you?

451
00:32:09,219 --> 00:32:10,345
Yu-jung?

452
00:32:11,513 --> 00:32:13,473
[rain pattering]

453
00:32:14,933 --> 00:32:16,643
[Wen] Your mom loved you
very much.

454
00:32:20,689 --> 00:32:23,150
She never wanted
to leave you behind.

455
00:32:28,947 --> 00:32:32,951
<i>Lu-yung's dad, Chou Chin-lai,
brought your mom
into Chang Xin.</i>

456
00:32:33,076 --> 00:32:35,745
[sighs] <i>He was like her mentor.</i>

457
00:32:37,164 --> 00:32:39,916
<i>Yu-jung was righteous.</i>

458
00:32:40,041 --> 00:32:43,461
<i>After she heard Chin-lai
say something was wrong
with the new oil,</i>

459
00:32:43,462 --> 00:32:45,672
<i>she kept investigating
the issue.</i>

460
00:32:56,725 --> 00:32:59,936
Chef, take a look
at this document.

461
00:33:00,061 --> 00:33:03,398
[dramatic music playing]

462
00:33:14,409 --> 00:33:15,494
[sighs deeply]

463
00:33:21,625 --> 00:33:23,001
Chin,

464
00:33:24,044 --> 00:33:25,629
do you have to involve me?

465
00:33:28,173 --> 00:33:30,509
You want me to be responsible
for what I've never done?

466
00:33:33,011 --> 00:33:34,179
[Yu-jung] Chef.

467
00:33:37,432 --> 00:33:38,642
Ta-chin,

468
00:33:38,767 --> 00:33:40,352
we've known each another
for so long.

469
00:33:40,477 --> 00:33:42,020
Don't do this, okay?

470
00:33:43,647 --> 00:33:47,817
Yu-jung, this has nothing
to do with you. Don't step in.

471
00:33:49,653 --> 00:33:51,655
How does this have
nothing to do with me?

472
00:33:51,780 --> 00:33:54,198
You just can't do that.

473
00:33:54,199 --> 00:33:56,201
- Where's your loyalty
to a friend?
- [Chang Ta-chin laughs]

474
00:33:56,326 --> 00:33:59,537
You sound noble. Loyalty?

475
00:33:59,538 --> 00:34:01,790
All you want is a price.

476
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:03,583
How much? Tell me.

477
00:34:05,460 --> 00:34:07,170
Am I that kind of woman to you?

478
00:34:08,797 --> 00:34:11,007
I've been with you
for so many years.

479
00:34:11,132 --> 00:34:13,176
Have I asked you for a title?

480
00:34:15,387 --> 00:34:17,680
You threw yourself at me.

481
00:34:17,681 --> 00:34:19,516
I've never forced you.

482
00:34:20,308 --> 00:34:21,351
[chuckles]

483
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:28,190
Chang Ta-chin,
you're not a man at all!

484
00:34:28,191 --> 00:34:31,360
[distorted]
I think I've been blind
all these years.

485
00:34:31,361 --> 00:34:34,030
Chef, I'll testify for you.

486
00:34:34,155 --> 00:34:37,408
We'll tell everyone
that you were framed.

487
00:34:37,409 --> 00:34:39,703
[dramatic music playing]

488
00:35:23,413 --> 00:35:24,873
Damn!

489
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:26,582
Chien-yuan!

490
00:35:26,583 --> 00:35:29,294
Stop that car! Now!

491
00:35:36,926 --> 00:35:39,471
[car honking]

492
00:35:44,768 --> 00:35:46,310
[inaudible]

493
00:35:46,311 --> 00:35:49,356
[suspenseful music playing]

494
00:35:50,940 --> 00:35:53,151
[car revving]

495
00:36:03,536 --> 00:36:05,789
[car crashing]

496
00:36:25,225 --> 00:36:26,309
[gasps]

497
00:36:35,568 --> 00:36:38,613
[soft dramatic music playing]

498
00:36:40,657 --> 00:36:43,701
[Wen] <i>I couldn't take you
to a hospital.</i>

499
00:36:43,702 --> 00:36:45,495
<i>I could only find
an underground doctor.</i>

500
00:36:46,413 --> 00:36:47,872
<i>The doctor told me</i>

501
00:36:48,665 --> 00:36:53,502
<i>it might be brain damage
or psychological factors</i>

502
00:36:53,503 --> 00:36:55,672
<i>that caused you to lose
your childhood memory.</i>

503
00:37:14,607 --> 00:37:16,942
[groaning]

504
00:37:16,943 --> 00:37:18,695
[coughing]

505
00:37:27,245 --> 00:37:28,955
[Wen] I've got rid
of the witness.

506
00:37:30,415 --> 00:37:31,916
[Chang Ta-chin] Whoa...

507
00:37:32,584 --> 00:37:33,835
So merciless?

508
00:37:35,462 --> 00:37:37,464
- I thought...
- [Chang Ta-chin]
What did you think?

509
00:37:38,298 --> 00:37:40,758
I don't know
what you're talking about.

510
00:37:40,759 --> 00:37:43,803
[laughs] Fine. Forget it.

511
00:37:47,307 --> 00:37:49,475
[Wen] <i>I took you to Tina.</i>

512
00:37:49,476 --> 00:37:53,605
<i>I was going to keep you
in the dark
about your true identity,</i>

513
00:37:53,730 --> 00:37:55,899
<i>so that you could
grow up happy.</i>

514
00:38:04,616 --> 00:38:05,909
[Yi-hsuan] I was going to

515
00:38:06,743 --> 00:38:09,496
just take the truth to my grave.

516
00:38:10,580 --> 00:38:12,707
You're dying anyway.

517
00:38:12,832 --> 00:38:17,628
But you dared to call us here
to watch you kneeling down
in front of us.

518
00:38:17,629 --> 00:38:19,714
I despise you!

519
00:38:23,009 --> 00:38:24,927
Do you know

520
00:38:24,928 --> 00:38:28,014
how painful it is
when I think of my mom?

521
00:38:29,432 --> 00:38:30,934
Who do you think you are?

522
00:38:32,060 --> 00:38:35,104
[dramatic music playing]

523
00:38:48,451 --> 00:38:50,620
Why are you
so much like your mom?

524
00:38:52,831 --> 00:38:54,040
Huh?

525
00:38:55,667 --> 00:38:58,628
When your mom was alive,
she betrayed me

526
00:38:58,753 --> 00:38:59,796
for Chin-lai.

527
00:39:00,839 --> 00:39:02,966
And now you've betrayed me
for his son.

528
00:39:03,967 --> 00:39:05,510
You both betrayed me.

529
00:39:07,512 --> 00:39:09,514
[laughs]

530
00:39:11,432 --> 00:39:14,853
You and your mom
are the greatest disgrace
of my life.

531
00:39:16,020 --> 00:39:17,480
Disgrace!

532
00:39:17,605 --> 00:39:19,357
[laughs]

533
00:39:20,567 --> 00:39:22,777
[dramatic music playing]

534
00:39:24,529 --> 00:39:25,822
I was wrong.

535
00:39:30,702 --> 00:39:32,495
Just rename it as you wish.

536
00:39:33,371 --> 00:39:34,914
It has nothing to do with me.

537
00:39:36,875 --> 00:39:38,834
To me,

538
00:39:38,835 --> 00:39:40,420
the name Chang Xin

539
00:39:40,962 --> 00:39:42,921
belongs to me, Chang Ta-chin.

540
00:39:42,922 --> 00:39:45,008
None of you are worthy of it.

541
00:39:49,679 --> 00:39:50,722
And you...

542
00:39:53,474 --> 00:39:56,019
I'll never see you
as my daughter.

543
00:39:58,771 --> 00:40:00,023
Having you...

544
00:40:01,441 --> 00:40:03,735
was a mistake
in the first place.

545
00:40:03,860 --> 00:40:05,111
I don't want to see you again.

546
00:40:07,196 --> 00:40:08,448
Get out.

547
00:40:10,199 --> 00:40:11,576
Out.

548
00:40:12,619 --> 00:40:13,578
Get out, all of you!

549
00:40:13,703 --> 00:40:15,163
[screaming]

550
00:40:20,710 --> 00:40:21,836
[flesh squelches]

551
00:40:36,142 --> 00:40:37,435
[groans]

552
00:40:49,447 --> 00:40:50,949
I'm sorry.

553
00:40:53,451 --> 00:40:54,744
[sobs]

554
00:40:57,956 --> 00:40:58,914
I'm fine.

555
00:40:58,915 --> 00:41:01,876
[soft dramatic music playing]

556
00:41:04,712 --> 00:41:06,047
Are you alright?

557
00:41:11,177 --> 00:41:13,179
[sobs]

558
00:41:21,938 --> 00:41:24,565
[Lu-yung] He's not worth
ruining our lives over.

559
00:41:30,738 --> 00:41:31,948
I'm sorry.

560
00:41:33,533 --> 00:41:35,493
I'm sorry.

561
00:41:35,618 --> 00:41:37,996
[music continues]

562
00:41:47,046 --> 00:41:48,589
[door slams]

563
00:42:11,154 --> 00:42:12,196
[sighs]

564
00:42:21,831 --> 00:42:22,999
Hi, bro.

565
00:42:25,251 --> 00:42:26,711
What?

566
00:42:28,171 --> 00:42:29,297
Here to laugh at me?

567
00:42:31,841 --> 00:42:33,676
If so, you can get lost now.

568
00:42:40,308 --> 00:42:41,684
Dad has cancer.

569
00:42:43,644 --> 00:42:45,897
He's in home hospice
care now. It's almost time.

570
00:42:49,942 --> 00:42:51,194
What does that mean?

571
00:42:53,821 --> 00:42:56,741
He didn't tell us
because he didn't want
to affect the stock price.

572
00:42:59,952 --> 00:43:01,287
It's getting worse fast.

573
00:43:07,710 --> 00:43:11,214
You can get out for 24 hours
to see him one last time.

574
00:43:22,225 --> 00:43:23,893
[machine beeping]

575
00:43:32,110 --> 00:43:33,236
Dad,

576
00:43:35,279 --> 00:43:36,906
I know you don't want

577
00:43:38,157 --> 00:43:40,159
to see yourself like this.

578
00:43:44,872 --> 00:43:45,957
You used to be

579
00:43:47,250 --> 00:43:48,918
the person I admired most.

580
00:43:51,671 --> 00:43:52,839
But not anymore...

581
00:43:53,923 --> 00:43:56,759
[emotional music playing]

582
00:43:59,762 --> 00:44:01,097
because you've...

583
00:44:06,269 --> 00:44:07,895
ruined my life.

584
00:44:21,742 --> 00:44:23,161
I hate you, Dad.

585
00:44:27,957 --> 00:44:29,417
I really hate you.

586
00:44:33,838 --> 00:44:35,423
[cries]

587
00:44:41,846 --> 00:44:43,681
[sniffles]

588
00:45:02,909 --> 00:45:04,994
[sobbing]

589
00:45:24,889 --> 00:45:28,517
- [birds chirping]
- [insects trilling]

590
00:45:39,320 --> 00:45:41,322
[sizzling]

591
00:45:43,407 --> 00:45:46,117
[pot scraping]

592
00:45:46,118 --> 00:45:49,789
[soft dramatic music playing]

593
00:46:06,514 --> 00:46:09,141
Come, help me fry an egg.

594
00:46:12,270 --> 00:46:13,896
[grunts]

595
00:46:46,262 --> 00:46:48,264
You've made great progress.

596
00:46:49,056 --> 00:46:51,434
[chuckles]

597
00:46:51,559 --> 00:46:53,269
You're exaggerating.

598
00:46:53,936 --> 00:46:55,062
[laughs]

599
00:46:58,316 --> 00:47:01,360
[music continues]

600
00:47:16,959 --> 00:47:18,294
You've grown up.

601
00:47:22,465 --> 00:47:26,176
Dad, I haven't cooked
with you for a long time.

602
00:47:26,177 --> 00:47:27,636
Want to taste my new dishes?

603
00:47:30,306 --> 00:47:32,057
Lu-yung,

604
00:47:32,058 --> 00:47:33,934
I live only in your dreams.

605
00:47:38,272 --> 00:47:39,440
Back then,

606
00:47:41,442 --> 00:47:43,235
it all happened so suddenly.

607
00:47:45,571 --> 00:47:48,199
There were things
I never got to tell you.

608
00:47:53,371 --> 00:47:54,497
Dad.

609
00:48:00,252 --> 00:48:03,046
I'm here to say goodbye

610
00:48:03,047 --> 00:48:04,548
to you properly.

611
00:48:06,967 --> 00:48:08,636
Stay with me, Dad.

612
00:48:14,433 --> 00:48:16,185
Live bravely on.

613
00:48:22,358 --> 00:48:24,527
And then, let go.

614
00:48:25,361 --> 00:48:27,029
[sobs]

615
00:48:30,324 --> 00:48:32,535
How can you say that so easily?

616
00:48:35,704 --> 00:48:37,415
It's not so easy.

617
00:48:38,541 --> 00:48:40,292
I've been practicing.

618
00:48:45,297 --> 00:48:46,382
Dad,

619
00:48:47,383 --> 00:48:49,051
if I knelt down back then,

620
00:48:50,469 --> 00:48:52,388
would you still be here with me?

621
00:49:00,020 --> 00:49:01,105
Lu-yung,

622
00:49:02,148 --> 00:49:05,526
there're some things
you can never lose.

623
00:49:08,237 --> 00:49:09,363
I'm proud of you.

624
00:49:12,741 --> 00:49:14,743
[music continues]

625
00:49:42,730 --> 00:49:45,733
[soft dramatic music playing]

626
00:50:18,349 --> 00:50:20,601
[upbeat music playing]

627
00:50:22,645 --> 00:50:24,355
[singer singing in Mandarin]

628
00:51:05,354 --> 00:51:09,440
[singer] <i>♪ Someone just
Like you lights up my dream ♪</i>

629
00:51:09,441 --> 00:51:12,194
[singing in Mandarin]

630
00:51:18,534 --> 00:51:21,579
[singer singing in Mandarin]

631
00:51:31,422 --> 00:51:32,714
[Yi-hsuan] So...

632
00:51:32,715 --> 00:51:34,465
have you booked
the bed and breakfast?

633
00:51:34,466 --> 00:51:37,094
[Lu-yung] Yes, of course.
It's so beautiful.

634
00:51:38,137 --> 00:51:39,596
Thanks.

635
00:51:39,597 --> 00:51:41,348
I'm looking forward to it.

636
00:51:42,683 --> 00:51:44,309
I don't know.

637
00:51:44,310 --> 00:51:46,270
It has been over ten years.

638
00:51:46,395 --> 00:51:48,731
It feels like I'm living
for the first time.

639
00:51:49,815 --> 00:51:51,108
Me too.

640
00:51:59,408 --> 00:52:00,534
I love you.

641
00:52:01,702 --> 00:52:03,245
I want to be with you forever.

642
00:52:05,581 --> 00:52:07,249
I'll think about it.

643
00:52:09,627 --> 00:52:11,753
[singer] <i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

644
00:52:11,754 --> 00:52:13,756
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

645
00:52:13,881 --> 00:52:16,133
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

646
00:52:16,258 --> 00:52:18,259
[singing in Mandarin]

647
00:52:18,260 --> 00:52:22,263
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

648
00:52:22,264 --> 00:52:25,309
[singing in Mandarin]

649
00:52:40,866 --> 00:52:43,911
[singer singing in Mandarin]
